WEBVTT

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.410
Kaibuki?

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.590
He's not at Shirobaco.
Can't reach his cell, either.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:26.290
"The Verbalism Club's New Trial Project

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:26.290
Silent Reading Theater Crane Edition"

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.720
Hayato, have you heard anything?

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.920
No. Why would you ask me?

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.790
"Shinji Hatano"

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.960
Well, everyone else is here.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:34.230
You could be sneaking out to go to a mixer for all I know!

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:37.130
Leaving me out, when I'm projected to be top of the popularity polls!

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:41.040
This is silly. Don't use secret lines to contact me for this.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.940
--I'm hanging up.
--Hold on, you--

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.310
"The Verbalism Club's New Trial Project

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.310
Silent Reading Theater Crane Edition"

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.910
They... won't be using their voices, huh?

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:53.150
Avant garde, no? You've just gotta try everything, meow!

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.920
Could it be that this is training

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.820
to use Verbalism Ability, even without their voices?

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:03.060
I like it! Let's use that as our excuse, meow!

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.630
Kujyo seems a bit down lately, don't you think?

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.630
Yeah, because he's too serious for his own good.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.430
There may be worries whirling around in his head.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:19.840
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:25.310
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:34.520
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:40.530
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief " look very similar</i>

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:45.930
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:51.710
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:58.050
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.950
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.890
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:08.790
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:14.230
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:20.300
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:25.740
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:31.750
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.680
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.420
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.360
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.190
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:50.600
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.910
"Flap! Bound Wings"

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.180
Repairs and upgrades on the
Vector are nearly complete.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.750
We've improved its ability to link with an M.J.B.K. as well.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:07.220
It's 100% safe...

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:13.760
...is what I'd like to say, but there are no absolutes when it comes to machines.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.250
You listening?

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.590
Writhing... What is this?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.700
Hello?

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:30.770
A word is being distorted...
It's "whirl" this time, huh?

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:35.640
But this is strange. It's different from all the other ones so far.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:35.580
"Whirl"

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:39.480
It's trying to be born from within a whirling vortex.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.880
Born?

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.890
Today, the keys have all gathered.
Is that what this means?

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:47.420
It's beginning to move.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:52.330
The great word which will eliminate all concepts.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:53.790
"Anti-M.J.B.K. Combat Tactics Draft Proposal"

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.970
Um, what's this thingy?

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.730
It's a proposal for an operation I've devised.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.070
I felt, in order to prepare for the unexpected,

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:05.640
we should consider countermeasures for all possible occurrences.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.140
You wrote this up yourself, meow?

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.480
I'd like you to read through it by tomorrow.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.950
I'm grateful, but aren't you pushing yourself a wee bit hard?

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:21.620
The only reason I joined the
Verbalism Club was to improve my voice,

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:25.760
because I believed doing so would be to my advantage as a politician.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.200
Yes, that's true.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.330
But, now that the M.J.B.K.s have become a concrete threat,

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.630
I have no intention of being lax in my response.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:36.100
This is a battle for the fate of our world.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.510
Do you understand that, Iwagami?

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.710
M-Me? Well, of course.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.050
In order to fight off and exterminate M.J.B.K.s,

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:48.150
it is quite natural that we should search for and devise the best possible plans.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.780
Am I wrong?

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.820
Nothing you've said is wrong.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:55.990
B-But things have worked out so far, you know?

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:58.460
There's no guarantee that will continue to be the case.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:01.700
But Akira always manages to handle it for us somehow.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:05.670
Are you going to keep clinging to him like that? To Kaibuki?

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.230
Hayato?

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.370
So that's a brand new brush, huh?

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:15.880
S-So you went to Sh-Shinjuku to buy that y-yesterday...

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:20.480
Yes, the craftsman is skilled, but he only has a storefront in Shinjuku.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:25.590
Well, it's fine to go out shopping, but let us know first, at least.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.020
I did notify you.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.090
I have a package for Shirobaco.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:31.580
Thank you.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.430
See?

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.430
"Left to go shopping

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.430
- Akira Kaibuki"

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:38.830
That's <i>so</i> not how you should be contacting us!

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.000
A-Akira, I-let's use our phones, okay?

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.540
Does the brush you use change things that much?

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:49.110
A good brush will write exactly what you want to convey.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:53.720
"Savior

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:53.720
- Akira Kaibuki"

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:51.210
It is through being written without hesitation

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:54.910
that the characters take on meaning and communicate their intent to others.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.020
You're writing way too many!

00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:00.590
"Savior"

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.690
--I'm trying out the pen.
--Just how much do you have to test it?

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:04.090
Ah! But maybe having one will work like a charm!

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.100
Yeah, maybe! Holding onto one might be okay.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.790
Maybe it'll make your Verbalism Ability hyper like Akira's, you know?

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.970
That's too many.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:21.530
Ah! Hayato! Look here!

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.480
What?

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:32.110
Sorry, but I'll be leaving early. I have an appointment with Mr. Hatano today.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.720
Huh? Hey!

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.450
Bro...?

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.660
Happy birthday.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.770
They're celebrating my birthday, huh?

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:56.300
But there's nothing from Dad this year, again...

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:05.980
What was that?

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.810
Mr. Hayashi! Where are you, Mr. Hayashi?

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.250
Dad?

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.970
Dad, something is coming.

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:21.270
Something incredibly big.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.670
Resonance?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:28.610
I see. It was inevitable that he would notice.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:31.950
The culture of words will soon meet its end.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:37.220
There is no means to resist it.
You need only remain quiet and watch.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.050
What do you mean?

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:41.990
Refrain from interfering.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:44.490
No! I can't do that!

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:48.500
I've decided I'll defeat him with my own hands and take Maia back!

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:52.500
I have to do it. Myself. With my own hands!

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:56.540
If you say something is coming to end it all, then I'm going right now!

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.730
I have to settle this before the end comes!

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.200
Fuu.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:10.720
What are you doing, Dad?!

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:13.150
Stay there until it's over.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:16.590
You could never win against the chosen one, anyway.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:19.330
Not against that man in that red Vector.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:21.490
No! The chosen one is...!

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:28.930
The distortion keeps growing.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:35.340
I had meant to wait and see what would be born.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:40.850
But to leave such a distortion and not set it free would be cruel.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:45.050
Let the curtains rise on the first act of ruin.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:51.290
I was worried what would happen during that imbroglio online,

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.590
but it looks like it was just a passing thing.

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:56.260
I'm relieved, Hatano.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.570
Sorry to have worried you.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:03.700
I hope you will continue to look after both myself and Kujyo going forward.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:05.270
Count on it.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:10.650
Using my base of support, it will be easy to get a promising young man elected.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:14.250
What a politician really needs is his base.

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:18.620
And your family has been in politics for generations.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.290
No voter base is as strong as the one you've inherited.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:25.130
My departed father... was a politician, as well.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:27.600
Oh, he was? What was his name?

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.230
Hanetaro Kujyo.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:33.940
He was elected once in Suginami,
Tokyo's 4th Ward, eight years ago.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.400
Just once, huh?

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:39.140
He was a classmate of
Foreign Minister Kobayakawa, I hear.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.980
At the time, they were considered two men who would carry the era.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:46.480
Kobayakawa... His meteoric rise was quite impressive.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.680
He really was an eloquent man.

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:52.450
No... He had a strength of words, you could say.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:54.860
Even if the logic and reasoning behind them was faulty,

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:58.330
there was something about his words that could move people.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:01.100
Without logic or reasoning...

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.800
My father was the opposite.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.100
He could be ineloquent at times,

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:05.500
"Voice ID

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:05.500
Akira Kaibuki"

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:08.100
but he wracked his brain to find ways to build a better future.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:11.040
He continued to propose sound political policies.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:16.140
It's true. Hanetaro worked hard up until the day he passed away.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:19.450
But he was unable to gain support and was defeated.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.320
I knew it.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:25.020
The reason I can't accept Kaibuki's methods...

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:28.020
Well, let's leave the serious talk at that for today.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.720
How about it? Do you have time?

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.460
I don't drink with just men.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.520
I know that.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:40.570
I'm underage, so I can't. Do you have milk?

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.570
Hey, why do you never pick me?

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:48.540
I do like how eager you are, but...

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.200
Huh? That's...

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:55.850
...Foreign Minister Kobayakawa's son, isn't it?

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.220
Mr. Ito?

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:01.060
Why, if it isn't Mr. Masatsugu Kobayakawa.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:02.890
To think I would meet you here.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:05.260
Um, Mr. Ito?

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:08.730
You remember me? I'm honored.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.270
He's inherited his father's presence, hasn't he?

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:14.770
He was born with a certain aura, you could say.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.700
Yes... He was.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.940
"History of Political Studies II"

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.940
"History of Political Studies III"

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.940
"Modern Politics"

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.940
"Conclusions on World Politics"

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.940
"Dictionary of Legal Terms"

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.520
Verbalize.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.730
Rejoice.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.590
I shall now set you free.

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:09.620
Uzu. Uzu!

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:13.290
"Whirl"

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:13.460
Uzu. Uuuuzu.

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.130
An e-mail? It's not in my inbox.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:21.640
Um, that e-mail seems to have come to me.

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.070
Why?

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:25.510
Get over here quick!
Our house has been burgled!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.780
Huh? We sell tempura here, buddy.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.970
But I dialed the police!

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:32.580
"Quantum Mechanics"

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:37.790
Hey! Why won't my e-mails go through?!

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:42.690
--I keep getting a different house when I call!
--I keep getting e-mails that make no sense. Is this a prank?

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:46.260
"Closed Due to Emergency

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:46.260
Sorry. Come again another time!"

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:45.490
Iwagami, call all the Verbalism Club members in for an emergency at once!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.430
Right!

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:48.290
Deava System, activate!

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:52.830
The damage is primarily to networks now.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:57.710
Data on the web is being linked to entirely different sites and servers.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:01.940
Without our Aquariphones, we'd have been unable to communicate.

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:03.780
Is it effecting the Deava base at all?

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:05.280
We're investigating that now.

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:06.780
This is...

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.820
There's an issue with the launch system.

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:11.350
Our data link to the inside of the gate is full of static.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.190
This is bad.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:14.790
Even if we launch Vectors,

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:18.060
we can't get them to the target
M.J.B.K. space like this.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.990
That sounds bad.

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:21.360
Worst case,

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:26.200
the Vectors would be stuck wandering inside the gate, having lost the exit.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.970
Th-That's terrible!

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:29.370
No problem.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.870
Come what may, I will always reach the enemy.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:33.970
For I am--

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:35.740
Stop! You sound like an idiot!

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:40.550
Big Brother...?

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.220
"For I am the savior," is it?

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:45.350
What basis do you have for saying that?

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:47.920
How can you say for certain that you'll reach the enemy?

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:51.690
Hey now, Hayato, what are you so worked up about?

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:54.230
If we end up wandering eternally, unable to make it there,

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:55.600
how will you take responsibility?

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:59.700
Are you so egotistical you'd put your own comrades' lives at risk?

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.840
Kaibuki, what do you mean when you say you're the savior?

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:05.930
What do you want from the world you'll save?

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.680
Is that everything?

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.550
What?

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.520
Your voice. Was that all of it?

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:18.190
--Page 225.
--Huh?

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:20.960
In the documents I gave you yesterday.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:25.190
There's a method to compensate for a failure in the launch gate there.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:28.300
Rewrite the program according to that.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.460
Is this it?

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:32.730
Wrack your brains and steadily work towards victory.

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:34.600
That is what a plan is.

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:41.400
Damn it!

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.540
What am I supposed to do?!

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:56.750
Whatever. If it's ending, that means
Maia will be coming back, right?

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:04.330
The red Vector will lose to Dad, and that'll be it. Serves him right.

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:17.680
"Akira Kaibuki"

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.990
I'm the one who should be with Maia.

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:38.430
You aren't.

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:40.300
Get away from Maia.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:46.440
Get away. Get away. Get away. Get away.

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:57.310
Get away!

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.510
Verbalize.

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:23.680
In manual mode, Iwagami will calculate the precise route to the gate.

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:26.080
We need to follow that.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:29.880
It's been so long. Gattai, Gattai.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.890
My Vector-5 and Karan's Vector-6 are the best suited for this.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.260
By analyzing the transformations of each Vector,

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:40.160
I simulated possible Gattai patterns.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:44.900
If we pair the Gattai of Vectors 5 and 6 with my and Karan's feelings,

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:48.570
it'll be possible to execute high-speed aerial maneuvers and cutting attacks.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.770
Incredible. He's figured all of this out!

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:51.770
Let's go.

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:55.610
Gattai, Gattai with Big Brother!

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.210
Bulk deployed. Quantum course calculated.

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:01.750
Bias multiplied. Alpha vector.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.950
Search category. Keywords fixed.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:05.550
Displaying ideal route.

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:06.850
Correction to coordinates.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:09.790
Y-axis, 2.4, X-axis, 0.8.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:13.930
Roger. Y-axis, 2.4, X-axis, 0.8.

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:16.200
Quanta distorted. Field stable.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:19.430
M.J.B.K. area has expanded to detectable range.

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:22.600
Gravitational waves detected. At 10 o'clock.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.440
--They made it out.
--Heck, yeah!

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:34.080
Uzu!!

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:37.550
So, it's a M.J.B.K. with a powerful magnetic field on a flat surface.

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:39.290
Then we just need to go above it!

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:41.390
Let's do it, Big Brother!

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:42.890
Sousei Gattai!

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:43.990
Fly!

00:17:43.990 --> 00:17:47.830
Aquarion!

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.280
"Gai"

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:03.980
Gai!

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:05.470
A gryphon.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:10.250
What? Our movement...!

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:14.150
Uzu!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.280
We can't control it very well!

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:25.600
Uzu!

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.000
It caught us!

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.100
This is ridiculous! We could have avoided that!

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:30.800
What are they doing?

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.040
They aren't bringing out their machines' full potential.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.110
Wh-Why?

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:37.950
Uzu!

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:39.050
Hayato!

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.510
The machine is heavy!

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:43.210
Why? Why won't you fly, Aquarion?!

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:48.160
Uzu...

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:57.800
Karan!

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:00.030
Hayato...

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.140
Karan! Karan!

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:06.570
Why won't it work? How am I inferior to him?

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:09.140
Your head is too heavy.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:12.750
You've got too much packed in there.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.210
Kaibuki.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:17.180
If you can't bear the weight, let it out.

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:21.560
Kujyo, what is it that's whirling around inside your head now?

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:26.060
That's what's weighing you down and binding your wings.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:29.000
Inside... my head...?

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.230
Let it out, Hayato Kujyo!

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:34.330
Right now, only your voice can save the world!

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.200
I●●●

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.440
Big Brother...

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.910
You look... like you're hurting...

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:45.870
I'm okay, so...

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.440
Karan...

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:53.890
I●●●

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:55.380
I...!

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:59.030
I've had enough!

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:03.300
I worked hard. I wracked my brains.
But nothing went well.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.870
Meanwhile, there's a guy who gets by without thinking at all!

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:09.100
It's not fair!

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:11.740
Is it wrong to approach things rationally?

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:13.910
Is it bad to be beholden to logic?

00:20:13.910 --> 00:20:18.710
I'm doing what I can, and I'm sick of getting nothing for it!

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:24.620
But what I'm most sick of is myself for thinking this.

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.950
Uzu!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:29.890
Did that lighten the load a little?

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:32.460
Whose fault do you think this is?

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.260
But right now...

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:40.730
...I can fly!

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:51.910
A lion soaring through the skies.
Those are Hayato's true feelings.

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:53.250
Hayato!

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:55.080
We're doing it, Karan!

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:55.520
"Hayato Kujyo" "Karan Uminagi"

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:06.190
"Wings of the Calm Wind"

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.300
Wings of the Calm Wind!

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:11.470
"Wings of the Calm Wind"

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.710
We did it, Big Brother!

00:21:34.490 --> 00:21:37.220
He just <i>had</i> to keep us on the edge of our seats.

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:40.160
Wait, this is...!

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:44.530
What? This isn't how it normally is!

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.580
What is that?!

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:00.010
Tornado Strike!

00:22:10.220 --> 00:22:12.730
Subete!

00:22:12.730 --> 00:22:16.420
We'll settle this, Akira Kaibuki.

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:40.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:50.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:50.930 --> 00:23:00.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:05.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:19.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:33.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:43.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:49.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:53.760
What does your father do for a living, Karan?

00:23:53.760 --> 00:23:56.700
He's in international business and is working abroad in Hamburg now.

00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:57.860
He's one of the elite!

00:23:57.860 --> 00:23:59.770
Aren't you lonely without him?

00:23:59.770 --> 00:24:01.470
He e-mails me everyday, so I'm just fine!

00:24:01.470 --> 00:24:04.670
Writing binds our hearts together even when we're apart!

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:07.540
Next time: Episode 12. "Bring Them Together! Heart and Heart."

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:07.510
"Episode 12: Bring Them Together!

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:07.510
Heart and Heart"

00:24:07.540 --> 00:24:10.480
Oh, I want to be with someone, too!
